    "text": "12 hours ago Some families plan road trips around museums or ballparks. Others plan them around a buffet line and a pan of peach cobbler. In Manchester, Tennessee, there is a small, old-fashioned diner where people happily drive close to two hours just to fill a plate with country cooking. Travelers with their GPS set for a big chain across the street have been known to change their minds at the last second and walk in here instead. Read full article\n3",
